common: do not turn a slow PSM sleep event into a firmware assert (T1100)

The freshly started WLAN firmware does not answer the PSM sleep event while it
is still initialising.  opfunc_pwr_sv() treated that as a fatal error and asked
STP to put the firmware into assert mode, so the firmware was shot in the back
a few seconds after WIFI_START, dumped its core and reset the whole chip - long
before it could raise WCIR_WLAN_READY.

Add a module parameter (default on) that only logs the timeout.  With the host
assert out of the way the firmware gets its full boot window.

--- a/common_main/core/wmt_core.c
+++ b/common_main/core/wmt_core.c
@@ -91,6 +91,13 @@
 /* #define CFG_WMT_BT_PORT2 (1) *//* BT Port 2 Feature. */
 #define CFG_CHECK_WMT_RESULT (1)
 
+/* T1100: the host used to turn a slow PSM sleep event into a firmware assert,
+ * which shot the freshly started WLAN firmware before it could raise READY. */
+static int t1100_no_host_assert = 1;
+module_param(t1100_no_host_assert, int, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(t1100_no_host_assert,
+		 "T1100: do not trigger a firmware assert when the PSM sleep event times out");
+
 /*******************************************************************************
 *                             D A T A   T Y P E S
 ********************************************************************************
@@ -1454,6 +1461,7 @@
 				("wmt_core: read SLEEP_EVT fail(%d) len(%d, %d), host trigger firmware assert\n",
 				 ret, u4_result, evt_len);
 
+			if (!t1100_no_host_assert)
 			wmt_lib_trigger_assert(WMTDRV_TYPE_WMT, 33);
 			goto pwr_sv_done;
 		}
